 [; #495 — the program renderer's map-key quoting converges on one shared
    rule (cx_emit_envelope_map_key, beside the data lane's cx_emit_map_key
    of #475): a key whose bare image would structurally mis-parse quotes on
    emit, so the emitted text re-parses to the same key (a bare `$tag`
    would read as a binding reference / reserved-envelope key; a bare
    `cx:seq` splits at the first colon). Bare names and auto-typing images
    stay bare — the `__cx_map__` envelope erases key types, so `{7: v}`
    (program-dc-entry-int-key) keeps its int-key image. Two cases pin both
    program render paths (map-as-element-child and map-as-top-result). ]

 [case id=program-map-key-quote-001-element-child level=core
  [tags map render emit quoting keys issue-495]
  [title $-leading / colon-bearing string map keys quote when the map renders as an element child]
  [in-cx [#
[ignored]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[m {'$tag': weird, 'cx:seq': v2, plain: ok}]
#]]
  [out-text [#
[m {'$tag': weird, 'cx:seq': v2, plain: ok}]
#]]
 ]

 [case id=program-map-key-quote-002-top-result level=core
