 [; §9.2 implicit operand propagation at truthiness boundaries (#346): an
    [err] reaching a condition slot short-circuits the form and surfaces as
    its result — it is never EBV-coerced (an err element would read truthy:
    items.len > 0). ENFORCED for [?if] (005-007). The guard/predicate
    boundaries — [?match] :when/:where, [?filter], [?partition], [?for]
    [where]/[take-while]/[drop-while] (008-014, gate=pending) — are an OPEN
    OWNER DECISION: shipped stdlib code (xap-dist registry lookups,
    validate shape walks) relies on err-valued guards meaning SKIP, while a
    uniform §9.2 reading says PROPAGATE. Do not enforce until decided. ]

 [case id=program-err-005-if-cond-err-propagates level=core
  [tags errors propagation if condition ebv]
  [in-cx [#
[ignored]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?if [/ 1 0] [then 'took-then'] [else 'took-else']]
#]]
  [out-text [#
[err code=cx-err:CXER0101 message='division by zero']
#]]
 ]

