 [; #1010: the row the issue names as its example. `3.0` is a DECIMAL literal,
    so what this pinned was decimal contamination of an int fold — the float
    reading is the twin below. Both matter: the two kinds contaminate to
    DIFFERENT results (`6.0` vs `6.0e0`), which is precisely what one row named
    for the wrong kind could not show. ]
 [case id=program-arith-decimal-contaminates level=core
