 [; #1010 — the DECIMAL half. Every row in this family used to be named
    `…-float-…` while carrying literals like `0.98` / `0.0`, which are DECIMAL
    literals: the family therefore pinned decimal EBV in every boolean position
    and left the float rule its comment cites (cxdm.md §6 rule 2) unpinned
    anywhere. The rows below keep their bodies under honest `…-decimal-…` ids;
    the `…-float-1NN-…` twins that follow are the same positions with
    e-exponent literals, which is what actually exercises the float reading.
    The two kinds agree on every verdict here — and that agreement is now a
    MEASURED result rather than an assumption the naming hid. ]

