cx-err:CXER0100
#]]
 ]

 [# ── [stream] → [lazy] RENAME (U1.1a, #763, stream-2 W2): `stream` is
       the delivery concept's name (delivery.md); the [?for] hint means
       lazy evaluation, so it is spelled [lazy]. Cutover, no dual-accept:
       the old spelling tombstone-errors loudly (same rule as the
       takewhile/dropwhile retirements above — a silent pattern-generator
       fallback would change meaning). ── #]
 [case id=program-for-lazy-001-hint-accepted level=core
  [tags for-comp lazy hint stream-2 U1-1a]
  [meta [#
note: [lazy] is an evaluation HINT (code.md section 7.4) — the yielded
note: values and their order are identical to the plain evaluation.
#]]
  [in-cx [#
[ignored]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?for [in $x (1, 2, 3)] [lazy] [yield [n $x]]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
[n 1]
[n 2]
[n 3]
#]]
 ]
 [case id=program-for-lazy-002-stream-retired-spelling-negative level=core
