 [case id=program-caps-001-c4-value-full-grant level=core
  [tags caps capability introspection C4 L104 stream-5]
  [; security.md C4 — the active capability set is exposed as an
     introspectable CX value: a canonical map over the closed nine-name
     list (granted-unscoped = true, scoped = a sorted scope sequence,
     ungranted = absent) + the private-range-policy field. The
     conformance runner grants in full, so this pins the L104
     normalization: the allow-all opt-out IS the explicit nine-grant
     form + private-range-allowed — one canonical form, not two. ]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[$caps]
#]]
  [out-text [#
{clock: true, env: true, eval: true, net: true, private-range-allowed: true, random: true, read: true, secret-reveal: true, subprocess: true, write: true}
#]]
 ]

 [case id=program-caps-002-value-reflects-narrowing level=core
  [tags caps capability introspection with-caps narrowing C4 L104 stream-5]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?with-caps [deny net] [deny subprocess] [deny secret-reveal] [$caps]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
{clock: true, env: true, eval: true, random: true, read: true, write: true}
#]]
 ]
note: narrowing is visible to the ACTIVE-set view — denied caps leave the
note: map (absent = ungranted, the canonical minimal form); a narrowed set
note: never carries the private-range-policy field.

