note: cx-err:CXER4113" — and its depth-cap TWIN (CXER4114) was enforced
note: while this half was not. It was worse than unenforced: the tree-eval
note: sub-env shares `state`, and [?lib] registers into
note: state.module_table, so a [?lib] inside an evaluated tree WIDENED THE
note: CALLER'S OWN module table as a side effect.
