 [case id=program-reserved-ns-001-cx-head-refused level=core
  [tags reserved-namespace cx-prefix negative E210 issue-820 issue-704]
  [meta [#
note: RULED 820-1a. The `cx:` prefix is reserved for the serializer's
note: canonical image. The DATA reader has always refused it; the PROGRAM
note: reader did not, so a program could construct and emit `[cx:x 1]` —
note: a document the data reader then refused to read back. Output failing
note: its own re-parse, the issue-704 class, through a door beside the
note: wall.
note:
note: Refused at CONSTRUCTION, not at emit: refusing on the way out would
note: let the bad node exist and be operated on first, and would point the
note: diagnostic at the emit site instead of at the name the author wrote.
note: E210 is reused rather than a new program-band code being minted — it
note: is ONE reservation, and two codes would teach a reader that
note: authoring `cx:foo` is two different mistakes depending on which
note: reader saw it first.
#]]
  [in-cx [#
[ignored]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[cx:x 1]
#]]
  [out-err [#
cx-err:CXER0100
#]]
 ]

