 [case id=program-cxpath-kindtest-010-text-takes-typed-scalars level=core
  [tags cxpath kind-test text scalar issue-809 ruled-809-1a]
  [meta [#
note: RULED 809-1a — `text()` takes BOTH character-data node kinds, Text
note: AND ScalarNode. cxdm.md §2.2 keeps them distinct Node KINDS, but
note: which one a body lands in is decided by AUTO-TYPING, not by the
note: author: this document's three values are a ScalarNode(int), a Text
note: and a ScalarNode(bool) from one authorial act each. Separating them
note: would make a result set depend on whether a value happened to
note: auto-type.
note:
note: This case previously pinned the NARROW reading (1, 7) as shipped,
note: deliberately, so the ruling would have a fixture to move rather
note: than a silent behaviour change. It moved. `node()` is unchanged at
note: 7 — it also takes the three elements and the root, which is why it
note: was never a substitute for a widened text().
#]]
  [in-cx [#
[doc [port 8080] [name Ann] [flag true]]
#]]
  [in-code [#
([$count //text()], [$count //node()])
#]]
  [out-text [#
(3, 7)
#]]
 ]

